cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below."
title: >-
  Learning to decode correlated quantum errors: a topological graph neural
  decoder that surpasses minimum-weight matching under structured circuit-level
  noise
authors:
  - family-names: Huynh
    given-names: Molena
    email: molena.huynh@jmp.com
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/molenahuynh/Topological-Graph-for-Decoding-in-QEC"
abstract: >-
  A learned surface-code decoder that matches minimum-weight perfect matching
  (MWPM) under independent circuit-level noise and beats it under structured
  correlated noise, benchmarked head-to-head against MWPM and BP+OSD on Stim
  circuits with paired statistics (Wilson intervals, McNemar, paired bootstrap).
  Part of the "spectral-truncation operators" (SpecOps) research program.
keywords:
  - quantum error correction
  - surface code
  - graph neural network
  - decoder
  - spectral-truncation operators
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Learning to decode correlated quantum errors: a topological graph neural
    decoder that surpasses minimum-weight matching under structured circuit-level
    noise
  authors:
